Docker Image pull error:
###########For docker image pull error(Error response from daemon: Get "https://registry.k8s.io/v2/": tls: failed to verify certificate: x509: certificate signed by unknown authority)
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/50768317/docker-pull-certificate-signed-by-unknown-authority
1. Create file /etc/docker/daemon.json
2. copy below content 
{
    "insecure-registries" : ["<registry-url>:443"] ----> try without 443 also if not works
}

Ex: 
{
    "insecure-registries" : ["registry.k8s.io", "asia.gcr.io", "gcr.io", "public.ecr.aws"]
}
3. systemctl restart docker
4. mkdir -p /etc/docker/certs.d/<registry-url>
5. ex +’/BEGIN CERTIFICATE/,/END CERTIFICATE/p’ <(echo | openssl s_client -showcerts -connect <registry-url>:443) -scq > /etc/docker/certs.d/<registry-url>/docker_registry.crt

Note: Kept 5th point in background and try to pull image.
